00:39:42,430 --> 00:39:43,305
TOBIAS COLDING: Yeah.

496
00:39:43,305 --> 00:39:45,290
That whenever--
so you would do--

497
00:39:45,290 --> 00:39:50,310
so what you would do here
is you would say Rk c,

498
00:39:50,310 --> 00:39:53,070
this here has to be bounded by--

499
00:39:53,070 --> 00:39:55,840
because x c is less than x.

500
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:59,880
So this is e to the x--
you have to eliminate c.

501
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:04,920
So you would do like
this, k factorial times x

502
00:40:04,920 --> 00:40:05,980
to the power k.

503
00:40:05,980 --> 00:40:10,400
You have to eliminate c because
you don't know anything really

504
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:11,600
about c.

505
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:15,920
And so this here now has
to be less than epsilon.

506
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:19,960
So now you only have--
you have fixed your k,

507
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:23,400
and so now you only have one
variable and you can solve that.

508
00:40:23,400 --> 00:40:26,220
But you really have
to eliminate c, yeah.

509
00:40:29,476 --> 00:40:29,976
OK.

510
00:40:32,664 --> 00:40:37,600
So again, so how well the
Taylor expansion approximate

511
00:40:37,600 --> 00:40:39,960
depends on the function.

512
00:40:39,960 --> 00:40:43,020
OK, the next topic is
another important topic.

513
00:40:43,020 --> 00:40:47,280
And so this is integrals.

514
00:40:47,280 --> 00:40:58,520
And there are different
ways of defining integrals.

515
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:07,280
This here is-- this is
certainly one of the--

516
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:10,720
maybe the most natural ones.

517
00:41:10,720 --> 00:41:15,040
And so this is what's
called Riemannese.

518
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:19,160
So it's after German
mathematician Riemann,

519
00:41:19,160 --> 00:41:19,980
integrals.

520
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:31,600
And so the thing is that here
now, you look at a function.

521
00:41:31,600 --> 00:41:37,800
You have a function on some
interval from a to b into R.

522
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:42,710
And this function
f here is bounded.

523
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:49,720
And the idea is--

524
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:52,940
so the idea is
for integrals is--

525
00:41:55,560 --> 00:41:58,680
so you have a function.

526
00:41:58,680 --> 00:42:01,920
And you want to be
able to define--

527
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:15,990
so define an area below graph.

528
00:42:18,880 --> 00:42:21,880
So if this has a
function, you want

529
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:26,680
to be able to calculate
what is this area.

530
00:42:26,680 --> 00:42:29,840
Now, if the function was to--

531
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:35,560
if the function was to
have crossed the x-axis,

532
00:42:35,560 --> 00:42:39,080
then this area here
would count negatively

533
00:42:39,080 --> 00:42:41,800
and this area here
would count positively.

534
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:42,720
Anyway.

535
00:42:42,720 --> 00:42:47,120
So this is what you want to do.

536
00:42:47,120 --> 00:42:51,890
And you're always starting
with a bounded function.

537
00:42:51,890 --> 00:42:54,740
Now, to do that--

538
00:42:54,740 --> 00:42:58,050
right, and so you
want to define that.

539
00:42:58,050 --> 00:43:01,680
The only thing that
you know for sure is--

540
00:43:04,810 --> 00:43:07,350
so there's only one
ingredient you have.

541
00:43:11,050 --> 00:43:26,440
So only thing you
know at the outset.

542
00:43:30,050 --> 00:43:35,290
So the only thing is that
if you take a right angle--

543
00:43:35,290 --> 00:43:37,160
so if this length here is--

544
00:43:41,050 --> 00:43:44,210
let's call it d,
and this here is e,

545
00:43:44,210 --> 00:43:48,490
then you know that
the area here--

546
00:43:48,490 --> 00:43:55,730
so area-- is d times e.

547
00:43:55,730 --> 00:43:59,250
That's the only thing we have.

548
00:43:59,250 --> 00:44:05,690
So now, how do we define
the area below the graph?

549
00:44:05,690 --> 00:44:10,382
And to do that, we first need
to talk about partitions.

550
00:44:18,170 --> 00:44:19,310
So partition.

551
00:44:23,410 --> 00:44:28,370
So suppose I have
an integral here.

552
00:44:28,370 --> 00:44:29,950
a and b are real numbers.

553
00:44:29,950 --> 00:44:32,130
So I have integral here.

554
00:44:32,130 --> 00:44:34,190
Then I talk about a partition.

555
00:44:39,330 --> 00:44:43,150
And it's useful to have
a notation for partition.

556
00:44:43,150 --> 00:44:50,340
So I call it P of
this interval here.

557
00:44:50,340 --> 00:44:59,510
This is finitely
many dividing points.

558
00:45:05,740 --> 00:45:10,460
And the dividing points always
have to start at a and end at b.

559
00:45:10,460 --> 00:45:14,140
So you have finitely
many-- let's say k many.

560
00:45:14,140 --> 00:45:19,300
And you're looking
at k plus 1 many.

561
00:45:19,300 --> 00:45:25,340
So the first one has to be a.

562
00:45:25,340 --> 00:45:34,864
And then you have x1 up to the
last one, and that has to be b.

563
00:45:37,940 --> 00:45:42,260
And so what you
are thinking about

564
00:45:42,260 --> 00:45:46,900
is-- so you have this
interval here from a to b,

565
00:45:46,900 --> 00:45:51,100
and you have these
dividing points.

566
00:45:51,100 --> 00:45:56,580
And you are thinking about
dividing the original interval

567
00:45:56,580 --> 00:45:58,780
into these subintervals.

568
00:45:58,780 --> 00:46:01,580
So these are the subintervals.

569
00:46:01,580 --> 00:46:19,040
So you divide the original
interval into subintervals.

570
00:46:23,660 --> 00:46:26,420
And the subintervals are--

571
00:46:26,420 --> 00:46:27,760
I'll do it like this.

572
00:46:27,760 --> 00:46:32,100
I will do it where I
take from-- it's always

573
00:46:32,100 --> 00:46:35,100
from one to the next.

574
00:46:35,100 --> 00:46:38,020
And I'll write it typically
where I'm starting--

575
00:46:38,020 --> 00:46:43,340
or I'm ending at i and
beginning at i minus 1.

576
00:46:43,340 --> 00:46:49,030
So I'm dividing it into
these subintervals.

577
00:46:49,030 --> 00:46:54,270
So in this case here, in this
case here where this is x0,

578
00:46:54,270 --> 00:47:00,590
there's going to
be k subintervals.

579
00:47:00,590 --> 00:47:05,450
And you only always go
from one to the next.

580
00:47:05,450 --> 00:47:10,870
So that's a partition.

581
00:47:10,870 --> 00:47:14,370
And now we need a second
notion related to this,

582
00:47:14,370 --> 00:47:16,210
and this is a subpartition.

583
00:47:23,950 --> 00:47:25,330
So subpartition.

584
00:47:29,390 --> 00:47:30,350
Subpartition.

585
00:47:30,350 --> 00:47:39,890
This is also sometimes
called a refinement.

586
00:47:44,190 --> 00:47:47,470
So a subpartition is-- so
if you have a partition--

587
00:47:47,470 --> 00:48:03,390
P1 is a partition, and then P2
is a subpartition of refinement

588
00:48:03,390 --> 00:48:21,910
if P2 has all the dividing
point of P1 and then some--

589
00:48:21,910 --> 00:48:23,150
and then some.

590
00:48:23,150 --> 00:48:26,270
I mean-- right.

591
00:48:26,270 --> 00:48:30,070
I mean, of course, it could be
a trivial subpartition where

592
00:48:30,070 --> 00:48:32,430
P1 and P2 are the same.

593
00:48:32,430 --> 00:48:33,870
That's OK.

594
00:48:33,870 --> 00:48:36,310
But in general, it will
have some more points-- also

595
00:48:36,310 --> 00:48:37,510
some more dividing points.

596
00:48:42,400 --> 00:48:46,820
Now, right.

597
00:48:46,820 --> 00:48:49,820
So now, let me look at--

598
00:48:49,820 --> 00:48:52,840
so what is, then--

599
00:48:52,840 --> 00:48:57,560
so now, let's try to get
closer to try to define this

600
00:48:57,560 --> 00:49:00,210
with the area below the graph.

601
00:49:09,112 --> 00:49:19,000
So again, we have a function
f from a to b into R.

602
00:49:19,000 --> 00:49:22,530
We assume that this
is-- so that is bounded.

603
00:49:30,240 --> 00:49:40,100
We have P here is a partition
of this interval here.

604
00:49:42,680 --> 00:49:47,240
Then we defined a
upper and a lower sum.

605
00:49:47,240 --> 00:50:06,660
Then we define upper and
lower sums as follows.

606
00:50:06,660 --> 00:50:09,640
So again, you have a given
function that is bounded

607
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,360
and you have a partition.

608
00:50:11,360 --> 00:50:13,760
And so we define
upper and lower sums,

609
00:50:13,760 --> 00:50:18,600
and the upper and lower sums
I will denote like this.

610
00:50:18,600 --> 00:50:21,040
It depends on the
function, of course,

611
00:50:21,040 --> 00:50:22,920
and then on the partition.

612
00:50:22,920 --> 00:50:24,880
That's an upper sum.

613
00:50:24,880 --> 00:50:28,460
And the lower sum, similarly,
I will denote like this.

614
00:50:33,695 --> 00:50:35,310
And so how are these defined?

615
00:50:39,610 --> 00:50:41,320
So they are defined as follows.

616
00:50:44,410 --> 00:50:50,770
That you have-- here, you have
your interval from a to b.

617
00:50:50,770 --> 00:50:56,170
Then you have-- this here
is x0; here, I have x1;

618
00:50:56,170 --> 00:50:58,370
and here, I have maybe x2.

619
00:50:58,370 --> 00:51:00,840
And then this thing here is x3.

620
00:51:04,930 --> 00:51:06,850
So I take--

621
00:51:06,850 --> 00:51:09,930
I look at one of
these intervals.

622
00:51:09,930 --> 00:51:12,310
Well, it could be this one here.

623
00:51:12,310 --> 00:51:19,690
It's between-- in this case,
it would be between x1 and x2.

624
00:51:19,690 --> 00:51:24,290
And I would look at the
function in this interval here,

625
00:51:24,290 --> 00:51:25,550
and I would--

626
00:51:25,550 --> 00:51:28,450
so the contribution
from this here

627
00:51:28,450 --> 00:51:36,730
would be that I would take-- so
for the upper sum with respect

628
00:51:36,730 --> 00:51:40,210
to this partition, the one that
comes from this subinterval

629
00:51:40,210 --> 00:51:51,150
here would be the sup of f
on this subinterval here.

630
00:51:53,690 --> 00:52:02,130
So the sup of the function
times the length of the interval

631
00:52:02,130 --> 00:52:03,090
like that.

632
00:52:03,090 --> 00:52:05,770
So this would be
the value that--

633
00:52:05,770 --> 00:52:08,990
in the upper that would
come-- in a minute

634
00:52:08,990 --> 00:52:11,130
I'll write it out more clearly.

635
00:52:11,130 --> 00:52:13,970
But this would be what
is coming from here.

636
00:52:13,970 --> 00:52:21,090
And likewise, for the lower
one, then the contribution

637
00:52:21,090 --> 00:52:23,730
from this little
interval here would be

638
00:52:23,730 --> 00:52:32,410
the inf of f, and then times.

639
00:52:32,410 --> 00:52:34,860
And the idea is--

640
00:52:34,860 --> 00:52:39,100
OK, so that would
be the contribution.

641
00:52:39,100 --> 00:52:41,970
The idea, of course,
is that you have--

642
00:52:48,460 --> 00:52:52,910
the only thing we knew was this
was the area of a right angle.

643
00:52:55,540 --> 00:52:59,180
And so you have
this function here,

644
00:52:59,180 --> 00:53:02,580
and you have some
little interval here

645
00:53:02,580 --> 00:53:06,060
between xi and xi minus--

646
00:53:06,060 --> 00:53:08,140
sorry, xi minus 1 and xi.

647
00:53:10,900 --> 00:53:15,342
And you're focusing on
this little interval here.

648
00:53:15,342 --> 00:53:16,800
And you're looking
at the function.

649
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:18,160
The function was bounded.

650
00:53:18,160 --> 00:53:20,500
So there is a sup on this.

651
00:53:20,500 --> 00:53:24,800
And you try to look
at the smallest right

652
00:53:24,800 --> 00:53:30,180
angle that kind of have
the graph that fits--

653
00:53:30,180 --> 00:53:32,580
where the graph
fits inside that.

654
00:53:32,580 --> 00:53:36,220
And then you're looking at--

655
00:53:36,220 --> 00:53:43,380
so this is the contribution
from this little interval to p--

656
00:53:43,380 --> 00:53:46,020
to the upper sum.

657
00:53:46,020 --> 00:53:51,580
And then you have that you're
looking at the largest right

658
00:53:51,580 --> 00:53:55,900
angle like this that
fits under the graph,

659
00:53:55,900 --> 00:54:00,940
and that's in contribution
to the lower one.

660
00:54:00,940 --> 00:54:05,740
And the idea is that if
the function is reasonable,

661
00:54:05,740 --> 00:54:08,460
if you're looking at
finite partition, then

662
00:54:08,460 --> 00:54:12,860
you should certainly get a
better approximation to the area

663
00:54:12,860 --> 00:54:13,960
below the graph.

664
00:54:13,960 --> 00:54:18,820
I mean-- and if the function
is reasonable, these two--

665
00:54:18,820 --> 00:54:21,860
OK, so now what is, then, the--

666
00:54:21,860 --> 00:54:24,220
let me just define this.

667
00:54:24,220 --> 00:54:31,340
So this thing here, it would
be convenient to the length

668
00:54:31,340 --> 00:54:35,530
of this interval to
denote it by this.

669
00:54:35,530 --> 00:54:39,030
So this is xi, xi minus 1.

670
00:54:39,030 --> 00:54:42,430
This is just the length
of that interval.

671
00:54:42,430 --> 00:54:42,930
OK.

672
00:54:42,930 --> 00:54:46,670
And so now written
out, this thing-- and--

673
00:54:46,670 --> 00:54:50,110
OK, let me make
one other notation.

674
00:54:50,110 --> 00:54:59,110
Mi is the sup of f
on xi minus 1 xi.

675
00:54:59,110 --> 00:55:01,310
That's capital Mi.

676
00:55:01,310 --> 00:55:13,110
And little mi is then the inf
on the same interval like that.

677
00:55:13,110 --> 00:55:18,310
And so the upper sum
for this partition, this

678
00:55:18,310 --> 00:55:30,350
is the sum from i equal to
1 to k of Mi times delta xi.

679
00:55:30,350 --> 00:55:32,510
That's the upper sum.

680
00:55:32,510 --> 00:55:44,710
And the lower sum is, then, the
sum from i equal to 1 to k of Mi

681
00:55:44,710 --> 00:55:46,990
delta xi.

682
00:55:46,990 --> 00:55:50,710
So that's the upper
and the lower sum.

683
00:55:50,710 --> 00:55:54,550
The first thing you observe
is-- the first thing

684
00:55:54,550 --> 00:55:57,800
you observe is a trivial fact.

685
00:56:00,390 --> 00:56:04,830
And it really should be the
case because one is like what

686
00:56:04,830 --> 00:56:07,430
fits inside the graph--

687
00:56:07,430 --> 00:56:10,590
below the graph, the
other is where the graph

688
00:56:10,590 --> 00:56:12,510
fits below the right angle.

689
00:56:12,510 --> 00:56:14,230
So you clearly have just--

690
00:56:14,230 --> 00:56:17,190
and this is just-- because
this number here is the inf,

691
00:56:17,190 --> 00:56:19,470
this is the sup on
the same interval.

692
00:56:19,470 --> 00:56:28,430
So you clearly have that L f,
P is less than or equal to U f,

693
00:56:28,430 --> 00:56:30,340
P. So this is--

694
00:56:33,040 --> 00:56:34,180
so this is clear.

695
00:56:37,520 --> 00:56:40,220
OK.

696
00:56:40,220 --> 00:56:46,010
Let's look at-- let's look
at a couple of examples.

697
00:56:52,080 --> 00:56:56,600
So just to make sure that
this is totally clear.

698
00:56:56,600 --> 00:56:58,270
Let me look at a
couple of examples.

699
00:57:01,040 --> 00:57:10,920
So the first example is--

700
00:57:10,920 --> 00:57:19,230
so I take a function f of x
equal to x squared plus 1.

701
00:57:22,040 --> 00:57:24,720
And my partition
and the interval

702
00:57:24,720 --> 00:57:29,530
here, I'm going to think about
this as a function on minus 2

703
00:57:29,530 --> 00:57:41,920
to 2 into R. And my partition
here is going to be minus 2

704
00:57:41,920 --> 00:57:45,980
minus 1, 0, 1, and 2.

705
00:57:48,880 --> 00:57:50,640
And, right.

706
00:57:50,640 --> 00:57:52,480
And so you have--

707
00:57:52,480 --> 00:57:53,220
so let's see.

708
00:57:53,220 --> 00:57:59,360
So this here-- so if I draw the
function, then this looks like--

709
00:57:59,360 --> 00:58:02,360
if this is 1--

710
00:58:02,360 --> 00:58:05,720
here, you have 1.

711
00:58:05,720 --> 00:58:08,160
Then it looks sort of like this.

712
00:58:08,160 --> 00:58:10,200
It doesn't-- more
or less like this.

713
00:58:12,880 --> 00:58:15,980
And so this means that
here and here, you have 2.

714
00:58:18,600 --> 00:58:20,580
And this here is minus 1.

715
00:58:23,320 --> 00:58:34,050
And here, you have minus 2.

716
00:58:34,050 --> 00:58:38,690
So now, if you're
looking at-- so, right.

717
00:58:38,690 --> 00:58:40,770
So this means here--

718
00:58:40,770 --> 00:58:42,970
right, so this is my partition.

719
00:58:42,970 --> 00:58:48,690
So this means that x0
is equal to minus 2.

720
00:58:48,690 --> 00:58:52,850
x1, that's the
next one, minus 1.

721
00:58:52,850 --> 00:58:56,650
x3 is the next one.

722
00:58:56,650 --> 00:58:57,970
That's 0.

723
00:58:57,970 --> 00:59:05,570
x4 is 1, and x5 is 2.

724
00:59:05,570 --> 00:59:09,370
And so, of course, all
of these intervals here,

725
00:59:09,370 --> 00:59:12,170
they all have the same
length in this case.

726
00:59:12,170 --> 00:59:20,210
So xi minus xi minus 1, this
was what we call delta xi.

727
00:59:20,210 --> 00:59:23,190
This here is, for each
of these, is equal to 1.

728
00:59:32,130 --> 00:59:35,480
And now, we have that the--

729
00:59:41,410 --> 00:59:44,650
and we have that the--

730
00:59:44,650 --> 00:59:48,570
when you're looking
between minus 2 and 2--

731
00:59:48,570 --> 00:59:50,730
sorry, minus 2 and minus 1--

732
00:59:50,730 --> 00:59:55,170
so in this interval
here, the function

733
00:59:55,170 --> 00:59:58,490
is-- the function on this
interval here is decreasing,

734
00:59:58,490 --> 01:00:04,570
so the largest value is
achieved at this point here.

735
01:00:04,570 --> 01:00:19,650
So M1, this is the same as the
sup of f between x0 and x1.

736
01:00:19,650 --> 01:00:26,980
And so this is the same as the
sup of minus 2 to negative 1

737
01:00:26,980 --> 01:00:28,540
right of f.

738
01:00:28,540 --> 01:00:32,580
And the function was decreasing,
so they lie on this interval.

739
01:00:32,580 --> 01:00:37,160
So the largest value is
achieved here, and that's 5.

740
01:00:37,160 --> 01:00:40,820
So this would be 5.

741
01:00:40,820 --> 01:00:45,740
And on the second
interval here, so this

742
01:00:45,740 --> 01:00:48,540
is between negative 1 and 0.

743
01:00:48,540 --> 01:00:51,820
Still decreasing, so the
value is-- the largest value

